    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "In a series circuit, current remains the same throughout, but total voltage is divided among components.",
        "In a parallel circuit, voltage across all branches is identical, but total current splits among branches.",
        "Soft iron is used to make electromagnets due to high retentivity and low coercivity, whereas steel is used for permanent magnets.",
        "Safety fuses are always connected in series with the live wire and have low melting points."
      ],
      "id": "3a4250j"
